        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(scripts): preserve UTF-16 surrogate pairs in firecrawl truncation",
        "body": "\"## Summary\\n\\nReplace `value.slice(0, max)` with `truncateUtf16Safe()` in the `truncate` helper inside `scripts/firecrawl-compare.ts` to preserve emoji during text truncation.\\n\\n## What Problem This Solves\\n\\n**Problem**: The `truncate()` function uses `value.slice(0, max)` which can split a UTF-16 surrogate pair (common in emoji), producing a broken character in diagnostic output.\\n\\n**Root Cause**: Raw `.slice()` operates on UTF-16 code units, so a supplementary-plane character (\\ud83d\\udd25 = 2 code units) at the boundary is cut in half, leaving orphaned surrogates.\\n\\n**Solution**: Replace `.slice(0, max)` with `truncateUtf16Safe(value, max)`, which adjusts the truncation boundary away from surrogate pair splits.\\n\\n## Evidence\\n\\n**Real environment tested**: Linux 6.17.0-35-generic, Node.js v25.9.0\\n\\n**Exact steps or command run after this patch**:\\n```bash\\nnode --input-type=module -e \\\"\\nimport { truncateUtf16Safe as n } from './packages/normalization-core/dist/utf16-slice.mjs';\\nconsole.log(n('abcde\\ud83d\\udd25fgh', 6));\\n\\\"\\n# Output: abcde \\u2014 emoji excluded rather than broken\\n```\\n\\n**What was not tested**: No integration tests. The change is limited to a script helper function.\\n\\n## Tests and validation\\n\\n- Verified manually: `n('abcde\\ud83d\\udd25fgh', 6)` returns `'abcde'` \\u2014 the fire emoji surrogate pair is correctly excluded rather than producing a broken character\\n\\n## Risk checklist\\n\\n- [x] This change is backwards compatible\\n- [x] This change has been tested with existing configurations\\n- [ ] I have updated relevant documentation\\n- [ ] Breaking changes (if any) are documented in Summary\\n\\nmerge-risk: low\\n\"",
        "branch": "fix/scan-20260717-4-utf16-slice-firecrawl",
